(5) Delegate any of the functions and powers granted under this article to such officers and agents as he may designate.
(Ord. No. 2012-3, 2-7-2012)

717:
For the purposes of this article, excess noise shall include:
(1) Sound emitted from a motor vehicle that is audible ten feet from the vehicle;
(2) Sound emitted from a building or dwelling that is audible at the property line of the building or dwelling;
(3) Sound emitted from other sources that is audible 100 feat from its source; and
(4) Any sound that registers 85 decibels or more at a distance of 100 feet from its source on a sound level meter or other instrument designed to measure sound level.

718:
The standards that may be considered in determining whether a violation of the provisions of this article exists may include, but not be limited to, the following:
(1) The level of the noise;
(2) The nature of the noise and whether it is usual or unusual;
(3) Whether the origin of the noise is natural or unnatural;
(4) The level and intensity of the background noise, if any;
(5) The proximity of the noise to residential sleeping facilities, hospitals, churches, facilities for the care of the elderly, ill or mentally ill, as well as any other area which historically is treated by the community as a quiet area;
(6) The density of the inhabitation of the area within which the noise emanates;
(7) The nature and zoning of the area within which the noise emanates;
(8) The time of day or night the noise occurs;
(9) Whether the noise is recurrent, intermittent, or constant.

